The following script plots the Maxwell-Boltzmann velocity distribution of
molecular oxygen and carbon dioxide at the same temperature.
% molecular masses of O2 and CO2
m_O2=5.31*10^-26;
m_CO2=7.32*10^-26;
k_B=1.38e-23; % Boltzmann constant
T=400; % temperature in K
%normalize the O2 and CO2 M-B distributions
norm_O2=4*pi*(m_O2/(2*pi*k_B*T))^(3/2);
norm_CO2=4*pi*(m_CO2/(2*pi*k_B*T))^(3/2);
v=1:10:2000; % velocity range in m/s
%compute the O2 and CO2 distributions
n_O2=norm_O2*(v.^2).*exp(-m_O2*v.^2/(2*k_B*T));
n_CO2=norm_CO2*(v.^2).*exp(-m_CO2*v.^2/(2*k_B*T));
%compare O2 and CO2 MB distributions at the same temperature
hold on
plot(v,n_O2,'-.k');

